# Local run — full Docker by default

Default product run is every service in its own container:

```bash
docker compose --env-file docker/.env up -d --build
# or
./deploy/scripts/present-platform.ps1
```

Atlas-only (no DB/broker): `./deploy/scripts/present-local.ps1` → `docker-compose.science.yml` → http://127.0.0.1:5080

Stop: `./deploy/scripts/stop-local.ps1` (volumes kept). Wipe: `docker compose --env-file docker/.env down -v`

## Verify without rebuilding the world

A one-line UI or API tweak does **not** need `up --build` of every image.

- Web only: `cd web-app && npm run dev` (or `npm run build`) against a running gateway
- Single .NET service: `dotnet build` / `dotnet run` in that project
- Order: `npx tsc` / `npm run check` in `order-service`
- If gateway is already at `localhost:5000`, curl it

Never rebuild ELK/Grafana (removed). Do not treat full-stack rebuild as the only way to confirm a landing/market/shop CSS change.
